nwang@black.clarku.edu (The freak) writes:
>Well, I always seem to run into trouble with them.  I can handle plain
>"giant ants" pretty easily.  However I always have trouble with soldier
>ants with their poisonous sting.  I always get killed by these unless I
>choose a Babarian or something with poison resistance, this is the
>1843278th time I have been killed by them at early levels (2 or 3).
>How should I deal with them if I don't have poison resistance or great
>armor/weapon?

There are no unique tactics to use against soldier ants.  They are the bane
of the lower levels.  Sometimes the best thing is to run like the dickens.

Don't forget the common evasive tactics:
  + walk through corridors with your pet in front of you
  + if you have telepathy, use it
  + the ol' dart-under-a-boulder trick might be worth trying
  + if the critter is far enough away, throw things at it.
    (soldier ants are *fast,* though.)
  + apply a mirror at the critter.  (a desperate move)
  + depending on your ethics, try "Elbereth" (another desperate move)

...Sometimes the game is determined that your character will die...

